ueries: standings by season (calculated), relegation, results.\n- Statistical analysis: avg goals per match, biggest wins, home vs away, best home/away record.\n- Team name normalization across variants (\"Palmeiras-SP\" vs \"Palmeiras\" vs full names).\n- Date parsing: ISO, Brazilian DD/MM/YYYY, with time.\n- UTF-8 handling.\n- BDD tests (pytest, GWT structured).\n- All 6 CSVs loadable and queryable.\n- Performance: simple <2s, aggregate <5s. So load CSVs once at startup and index in memory (pandas? no pandas in venv — only pytest. Let me check network availability to install mcp SDK. If no network, I write a pure-stdlib implementation).\n\nLet me check network access.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c64ae62001WvGdtasLx8qlL5","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c648e7b001DVDDFhmoCHddco"}}
