         print(\"client sees tools:\", [(t.name, t.description) for t in tools.tools])\n            res = await session.call_tool(\"greet\", {\"name\": \"world\"})\n            print(\"result:\", res.content[0].text)\n\nasyncio.run(main())\nEOF","time":{"start":1788256581797,"end":1788256581837}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The mcp 2.x API works: `MCPServer`, `@server.tool()`, `list_tools()` → list, `call_tool(name, args)` → CallToolResult with content and structured_content.\n\nNow, let me verify a real stdio end-to-end session using the client library, to make sure the server actually works over the wire for the integration test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c65eac2001rIBEb6KrQJWDrX","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c65e108001a8yNIzEbHghhY7"}}
