{"type":"text","timestamp":1788256701061,"sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","part":{"id":"prt_05c679166001mGdPb9YSFXKK6D","messageID":"msg_05c675c460017XZ7vkUZqkIYBb","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","type":"text","text":"Key findings: BRF (2014-2023) overlaps the other Brasileirão/Copa files, spellings differ across files (`Athletico-PR` vs `Atletico-PR`, `Vasco da Gama` vs `Vasco`), Copa final = round 8, Libertadores has `final` stage + one `NA` season. Let me prototype the dedupe+standings logic to validate the approach and extract ground-truth numbers for tests.","time":{"start":1788256686438,"end":1788256701058}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788256701300,"sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a2992eaf12920e4c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\ndef rows(p):\n    with open(p, encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nUF = {'AC','AL','AP','AM','BA','CE','DF','ES','GO','MA','MT','MS','MG','PA','PB','PR','PE','PI','RJ','RN','RS','RO','RR','SC','SP','SE','TO'}\nALIAS = {'athletico pr':'atletico pr', 'vasco da gama':'vasco'}\n\ndef deacc(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\ndef norm(name):\n    s = deacc(name).lower().replace('.', ' ')\n    s = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', s).strip()\n    for _ in range(2):\n        m = re.search(r'(?:^|\\s)[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', s)\n        if m and m.group(1).upper() in UF:\n            s = s[:m.start()].strip()\n        s = re.sub(r'\\s*[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', '', s) if re.search(r'[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', s) and re.search(r'[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', s).group(1).upper() in UF else s\n    return ALIAS.get(s, s)\n\nbra = rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nhist = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\n\ndef to_int(v):\n    v = v.strip()\n    return int(float(v)) if v and v not in ('NA','-','') else None\n\nseen = {}\nmatches = []\ndef add(date, home, away, hg, ag, season, src):\n    k = (date, norm(home), norm(away))\n    if k in seen: return\n    seen[k] = src\n    matches.append((date, norm(home), norm(away), hg, ag, int(season), src))\n\nfor r in bra:\n    add(r['datetime'][:10], r['home_team'], r['away_team'], to_int(r['home_goal']), to_int(r['away_goal']), r['season'], 'bra')\nfor r in hist:\n    d = datetime.strptime(r['Data'], '%d/%m/%Y').strftime('%Y-%m-%d')\n    add(d, r['Equipe_mandante'], r['Equipe_visitante'], to_int(r['Gols_mandante']), to_int(r['Gols_visitante']), r['Ano'], 'hist')\nfor r in bf:\n    if r['tournament'] == 'Serie A':\n        add(r['date'], r['home'], r['away'], to_int(r['home_goal']), to_int(r['away_goal']), r['date'][:4], 'brf')\n\n# per-season counts after dedupe\nsc = defaultdict(int)\nfor m in matches: sc[m[5]] += 1\nprint(\"serie_a dedup per season:\", dict(sorted(sc.items())))\n\n# 2019 standings\ndef standings(season):\n    tbl = defaultdict(lambda: [0,0,0,0,0])  # pts,w,d,l,gf,ga\n    for date, h, a, hg, ag, s, src in matches:\n        if s != season or hg is None or ag is None: continue\n        for team, gf, ga_ in ((h,hg,ag),(a,ag,hg)):\n            t = tbl[team]; t[3]+=1; t[4]+=gf; t[5]+=ga_\n            if gf > ga_: t[0]+=3; t[1]+=1\n            elif gf == ga_: t[0]+=1; t[2]+=1\n            else: t[3]+=1\n    return sorted(tbl.items(), key=lambda x: (-x[1][0], -(x[1][4]-x[1][5])))\n\nprint(\"\\n2019 Serie A top 5:\")\nfor team, (pts,w,d,l,gf,ga) in standings(2019)[:5]:\n    print(f\"  {team}: {pts} pts ({w}W {d}D {l}L) GF{gf} GA{ga}\")\nprint(\"2019 bottom 4:\", [t for t,_ in standings(2019)[-4:]])\nprint(\"\\n2020 bottom 4:\", [t for t,_ in standings(2020)[-4:]])\nprint(\"\\n2021 count check (BRF alone 491):\", sum(1 for m in matches if m[5]==2021))\n# Fla-Flu 2023-09-03 in BRF?\nflaflu = [m for m in matches if m[5]==2023 and {m[1],m[2]}=={'flamengo','fluminense'}]\nprint(\"\\nFla-Flu 2023 matches:\", flaflu[:4], \"total:\", len(flaflu))\n# BRF internal dupes 2021\nk = defaultdict(int)\nfor r in bf:\n    if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2021':\n        k[(r['date'], norm(r['home']), norm(r['away']))] += 1\ndups = {kk:v for kk,v in k.items() if v>1}\nprint(\"BRF 2021 Serie A internal duplicate keys:\", len(dups), list(dups.items())[:3])\nEOF"},"output":"serie_a dedup per season: {2003: 552, 2004: 552, 2005: 462, 2006: 380, 2007: 380, 2008: 380, 2009: 380, 2010: 380, 2011: 380, 2012: 380, 2013: 418, 2014: 574, 2015: 606, 2016: 655, 2017: 673, 2018: 719, 2019: 661, 2020: 588, 2021: 775, 2022: 666, 2023: 377}\n\n2019 Serie A top 5:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 68, in <module>\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 61, in standings\nIndexError: list index out of range\n","metadata":{"output":"serie_a dedup per season: {2003: 552, 2004: 552, 2005: 462, 2006: 380, 2007: 380, 2008: 380, 2009: 380, 2010: 380, 2011: 380, 2012: 380, 2013: 418, 2014: 574, 2015: 606, 2016: 655, 2017: 673, 2018: 719, 2019: 661, 2020: 588, 2021: 775, 2022: 666, 2023: 377}\n\n2019 Serie A top 5:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 68, in <module>\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 61, in standings\nIndexError: list index out of range\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\ndef rows(p):\n    with open(p, encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nUF = {'AC','AL','AP','AM','BA','CE','DF','ES','GO','MA','MT','MS','MG','PA','PB','PR','PE','PI','RJ','RN','RS','RO','RR','SC','SP','SE','TO'}\nALIAS = {'athletico pr':'atletico pr', 'vasco da gama':'vasco'}\n\ndef deacc(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\ndef norm(name):\n    s = deacc(name).lower().replace('.', ' ')\n    s = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', s).strip()\n    for _ in range(2):\n        m = re.search(r'(?:^|\\s)[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', s)\n        if m and m.group(1).upper() in UF:\n            s = s[:m.start()].strip()\n        s = re.sub(r'\\s*[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', '', s) if re.search(r'[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', s) and re.search(r'[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', s).group(1).upper() in UF else s\n    return ALIAS.get(s, s)\n\nbra = rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nhist = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\n\ndef to_int(v):\n    v = v.strip()\n    return int(float(v)) if v and v not in ('NA','-','') else None\n\nseen = {}\nmatches = []\ndef add(date, home, away, hg, ag, season, src):\n    k = (date, norm(home), norm(away))\n    if k in seen: return\n    seen[k] = src\n    matches.append((date, norm(home), norm(away), hg, ag, int(season), src))\n\nfor r in bra:\n    add(r['datetime'][:10], r['home_team'], r['away_team'], to_int(r['home_goal']), to_int(r['away_goal']), r['season'], 'bra')\nfor r in hist:\n    d = datetime.strptime(r['Data'], '%d/%m/%Y').strftime('%Y-%m-%d')\n    add(d, r['Equipe_mandante'], r['Equipe_visitante'], to_int(r['Gols_mandante']), to_int(r['Gols_visitante']), r['Ano'], 'hist')\nfor r in bf:\n    if r['tournament'] == 'Serie A':\n        add(r['date'], r['home'], r['away'], to_int(r['home_goal']), to_int(r['away_goal']), r['date'][:4], 'brf')\n\n# per-season counts after dedupe\nsc = defaultdict(int)\nfor m in matches: sc[m[5]] += 1\nprint(\"serie_a dedup per season:\", dict(sorted(sc.items())))\n\n# 2019 standings\ndef standings(season):\n    tbl = defaultdict(lambda: [0,0,0,0,0])  # pts,w,d,l,gf,ga\n    for date, h, a, hg, ag, s, src in matches:\n        if s != season or hg is None or ag is None: continue\n        for team, gf, ga_ in ((h,hg,ag),(a,ag,hg)):\n            t = tbl[team]; t[3]+=1; t[4]+=gf; t[5]+=ga_\n            if gf > ga_: t[0]+=3; t[1]+=1\n            elif gf == ga_: t[0]+=1; t[2]+=1\n            else: t[3]+=1\n    return sorted(tbl.items(), key=lambda x: (-x[1][0], -(x[1][4]-x[1][5])))\n\nprint(\"\\n2019 Serie A top 5:\")\nfor team, (pts,w,d,l,gf,ga) in standings(2019)[:5]:\n    print(f\"  {team}: {pts} pts ({w}W {d}D {l}L) GF{gf} GA{ga}\")\nprint(\"2019 bottom 4:\", [t for t,_ in standings(2019)[-4:]])\nprint(\"\\n2020 bottom 4:\", [t for t,_ in standings(2020)[-4:]])\nprint(\"\\n2021 count check (BRF alone 491):\", sum(1 for m in matches if m[5]==2021))\n# Fla-Flu 2023-09-03 in BRF?\nflaflu = [m for m in matches if m[5]==2023 and {m[1],m[2]}=={'flamengo','fluminense'}]\nprint(\"\\nFla-Flu 2023 matches:\", flaflu[:4], \"total:\", len(flaflu))\n# BRF internal dupes 2021\nk = defaultdict(int)\nfor r in bf:\n    if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2021':\n        k[(r['date'], norm(r['home']), norm(r['away']))] += 1\ndups = {kk:v for kk,v in k.items() if v>1}\nprint(\"BRF 2021 Serie A internal duplicate keys:\", len(dups), list(dups.items())[:3])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788256701294,"end":1788256701299}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Very important findings:\n\n1. **BRF covers 2014-2023** — so BRF \"Serie A\" overlaps Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2022) in 2014-2022 AND extends to 2023. BRF Copa do Brasil (2014-2023) overlaps Brazilian_Cup (2012-2021) in 2014-2021. So dedupe across files is essential. Note BRF 2015 Serie A has 378 (2 missing), 2020 264 (incomplete), 2021 491 (?? more than 380 — maybe includes duplicated rows or extra?), 2023 377. Hmm 491 in 2021 — weird, maybe duplicates within BRF itself. Dedupe handles it.\n\n2. **BRAS 2019 vs HIST 2019 team spellings differ**: \"Atletico-PR\" vs \"Athletico-PR\", \"Avai-SC\" vs \"Avaí\", \"Gremio-RS\" vs \"Grêmio\", \"Sao Paulo-SP\" vs \"São Paulo\", \"Csa-AL\" vs \"CSA\", \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" vs \"Vasco\". So alias mapping needed:\n   - \"athletico pr\" ↔ \"atletico pr\" (same club, renamed 2019)\n   - \"vasco da gama\" ↔ \"vasco\"\n   Accent stripping + UF removal handles: Avai/Avaí, Gremio/Grêmio, Sao Paulo/São Paulo, CSA/Csa. \n\n   Dedupe key must use canonical key with these aliases applied, or 2019 would double-count.\n\n3. **Copa rounds 1-8** — round 8 = final (14 matches over seasons... wait final should be 2 matches per season (two legs) — rounds: 2012-2021: round 8 appears 14 times total. E.g., seasons 2012,2013,...? Counter over all seasons: '8': 14. So maybe 7 seasons × 2 legs. And round 7 = semifinal (30 = maybe 15 pairs?). For \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" → stage=\"8\"? I'll expose a `round` filter and document in competition_info that the final is round 8 (and provide `search_matches(competition='copa_do_brasil', stage='8')`). Let me verify: which seasons have round 8?\n\n4. **LIB finals**: 2 matches per season 2013-2018 (two legs), 1 from 2019+ (single final). stage='final' works directly.\n\n5. **2023 coverage**: only BRF has 2023 (Serie A 377, Serie B 380, Serie C 215, Copa 116). So \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\" → BRF Serie A 2023. And spec's example \"2023-09-03: Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense\" should be in BRF. Let me verify.\n\n6. **Libertadores has 'NA' season (1 row)** — handle missing season.\n\nNow verify dedupe + standings computation with a quick prototype script (before writing the real code, validate the approach and get ground truth numbers for tests):\n- Combine BRAS + HIST + BRF-SerieA → dedupe → per-season counts; 2019 should be 380 → standings: Flamengo 90 pts.\n- Check 2021 BRF Serie A 491 rows — dupes within BRF?\n- Check Copa final round per season.\n- Check Fla-Flu 2023-09-03 exists in BRF.\n- FIFA club names for Flamengo / São Paulo — check exact strings.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c6795b8001bDp1XJMLIYwZOB","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c675c460017XZ7vkUZqkIYBb"}}
