{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788256726734,"sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-ae34555e5cca5dce","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef rows(p):\n    with open(p, encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nUF = {'AC','AL','AP','AM','BA','CE','DF','ES','GO','MA','MT','MS','MG','PA','PB','PR','PE','PI','RJ','RN','RS','RO','RR','SC','SP','SE','TO'}\nALIAS = {'athletico pr':'atletico pr', 'vasco da gama':'vasco'}\n\ndef deacc(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\ndef norm(name):\n    s = deacc(name).lower().replace('.', ' ')\n    s = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', s).strip()\n    s = re.sub(r'\\s*[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', lambda m: '' if m.group(1).upper() in UF else m.group(0), s)\n    return ALIAS.get(s, s)\n\nbra = rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nhist = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\n\n# 2013: BRAS vs HIST — which keys don't match?\nbra13 = {(r['datetime'][:10], norm(r['home_team']), norm(r['away_team'])): r for r in bra if r['season']=='2013'}\nhist13 = {(datetime.strptime(r['Data'], '%d/%m/%Y').strftime('%Y-%m-%d'), norm(r['Equipe_mandante']), norm(r['Equipe_visitante'])): r for r in hist if r['Ano']=='2013'}\nprint(\"bras13:\", len(bra13), \"hist13:\", len(hist13), \"common:\", len(set(bra13)&set(hist13)))\nunm_b = set(bra13) - set(hist13)\nunm_h = set(hist13) - set(bra13)\nprint(\"unmatched bras:\", len(unm_b), \"unmatched hist:\", len(unm_h))\n# near-miss: same teams, different date\nh_by_teams = defaultdict(list)\nfor k in hist13: h_by_teams[(k[1],k[2])].append(k[0])\nnear = 0\nfor (d,h,a) in unm_b:\n    if (h,a) in h_by_teams:\n        for d2 in h_by_teams[(h,a)]:\n            dd = (datetime.strptime(d,'%Y-%m-%d') - datetime.strptime(d2,'%Y-%m-%d')).days\n            if abs(dd) <= 3:\n                near += 1\n                if near <= 5: print(\"  NEAR MISS:\", d, h, a, \"vs hist date\", d2, \"delta\", dd)\n                break\nprint(\"near-miss (same teams, |delta date| <= 3):\", near)\nprint(\"sample unmatched bras keys:\", list(unm_b)[:6])\nprint(\"sample unmatched hist keys:\", list(unm_h)[:6])\n# team key sets diff\nbt = {k[1] for k in bra13} | {k[2] for k in bra13}\nht = {k[1] for k in hist13} | {k[2] for k in hist13}\nprint(\"teams only in bras13:\", bt - ht)\nprint(\"teams only in hist13:\", ht - bt)\nEOF"},"output":"bras13: 380 hist13: 380 common: 342\nunmatched bras: 38 unmatched hist: 38\nnear-miss (same teams, |delta date| <= 3): 0\nsample unmatched bras keys: [('2013-09-22', 'atletico', 'ponte preta'), ('2013-07-27', 'portuguesa', 'atletico'), ('2013-11-03', 'atletico', 'internacional'), ('2013-11-10', 'atletico', 'sao paulo'), ('2013-10-16', 'atletico', 'atletico'), ('2013-05-26', 'fluminense', 'atletico')]\nsample unmatched hist keys: [('2013-09-04', 'athletico', 'santos'), ('2013-11-24', 'athletico', 'nautico'), ('2013-09-22', 'athletico', 'ponte preta'), ('2013-08-07', 'athletico', 'bahia'), ('2013-10-13', 'athletico', 'portuguesa'), ('2013-10-09', 'corinthians', 'athletico')]\nteams only in bras13: set()\nteams only in hist13: {'athletico'}\n","metadata":{"output":"bras13: 380 hist13: 380 common: 342\nunmatched bras: 38 unmatched hist: 38\nnear-miss (same teams, |delta date| <= 3): 0\nsample unmatched bras keys: [('2013-09-22', 'atletico', 'ponte preta'), ('2013-07-27', 'portuguesa', 'atletico'), ('2013-11-03', 'atletico', 'internacional'), ('2013-11-10', 'atletico', 'sao paulo'), ('2013-10-16', 'atletico', 'atletico'), ('2013-05-26', 'fluminense', 'atletico')]\nsample unmatched hist keys: [('2013-09-04', 'athletico', 'santos'), ('2013-11-24', 'athletico', 'nautico'), ('2013-09-22', 'athletico', 'ponte preta'), ('2013-08-07', 'athletico', 'bahia'), ('2013-10-13', 'athletico', 'portuguesa'), ('2013-10-09', 'corinthians', 'athletico')]\nteams only in bras13: set()\nteams only in hist13: {'athletico'}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef rows(p):\n    with open(p, encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nUF = {'AC','AL','AP','AM','BA','CE','DF','ES','GO','MA','MT','MS','MG','PA','PB','PR','PE','PI','RJ','RN','RS','RO','RR','SC','SP','SE','TO'}\nALIAS = {'athletico pr':'atletico pr', 'vasco da gama':'vasco'}\n\ndef deacc(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\ndef norm(name):\n    s = deacc(name).lower().replace('.', ' ')\n    s = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', s).strip()\n    s = re.sub(r'\\s*[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', lambda m: '' if m.group(1).upper() in UF else m.group(0), s)\n    return ALIAS.get(s, s)\n\nbra = rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nhist = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\n\n# 2013: BRAS vs HIST — which keys don't match?\nbra13 = {(r['datetime'][:10], norm(r['home_team']), norm(r['away_team'])): r for r in bra if r['season']=='2013'}\nhist13 = {(datetime.strptime(r['Data'], '%d/%m/%Y').strftime('%Y-%m-%d'), norm(r['Equipe_mandante']), norm(r['Equipe_visitante'])): r for r in hist if r['Ano']=='2013'}\nprint(\"bras13:\", len(bra13), \"hist13:\", len(hist13), \"common:\", len(set(bra13)&set(hist13)))\nunm_b = set(bra13) - set(hist13)\nunm_h = set(hist13) - set(bra13)\nprint(\"unmatched bras:\", len(unm_b), \"unmatched hist:\", len(unm_h))\n# near-miss: same teams, different date\nh_by_teams = defaultdict(list)\nfor k in hist13: h_by_teams[(k[1],k[2])].append(k[0])\nnear = 0\nfor (d,h,a) in unm_b:\n    if (h,a) in h_by_teams:\n        for d2 in h_by_teams[(h,a)]:\n            dd = (datetime.strptime(d,'%Y-%m-%d') - datetime.strptime(d2,'%Y-%m-%d')).days\n            if abs(dd) <= 3:\n                near += 1\n                if near <= 5: print(\"  NEAR MISS:\", d, h, a, \"vs hist date\", d2, \"delta\", dd)\n                break\nprint(\"near-miss (same teams, |delta date| <= 3):\", near)\nprint(\"sample unmatched bras keys:\", list(unm_b)[:6])\nprint(\"sample unmatched hist keys:\", list(unm_h)[:6])\n# team key sets diff\nbt = {k[1] for k in bra13} | {k[2] for k in bra13}\nht = {k[1] for k in hist13} | {k[2] for k in hist13}\nprint(\"teams only in bras13:\", bt - ht)\nprint(\"teams only in hist13:\", ht - bt)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788256726728,"end":1788256726733}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Two bugs in my prototype:\n\n1. The standings tuple: `t[3]+=1` for matches played — I initialized 5 slots [pts,w,d,l?...] wait I wrote `defaultdict(lambda: [0,0,0,0,0])` — 5 elements, indices 0-4, but I use t[5]. Need 6 elements. Fix: `[0]*6`.\n\n2. **Bigger issue**: dedup per season shows 2014: 574, 2015: 606... NOT 380! The BRAS file and HIST file both have 2014 with 380 each — that's only 380 after dedupe if keys match. But I'm getting 574 for 2014 — meaning keys don't match. Why? The HIST file dates are DD/MM/YYYY — I parse to YYYY-MM-DD. BRAS datetime \"2014-05-19 18:30:00\"[:10] → same. Team names... maybe differing: e.g., BRAS uses \"Atletico-PR\" and HIST 2014 uses \"Atlético-PR\" — both normalize to \"atletico pr\" ✓. Hmm, but maybe HIST has \"Vasco\" vs BRAS \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → \"vasco da gama\" vs \"vasco\" — alias handles.\n\nWait, the problem could be that matches differ in *which* team is home/away? Same match should have same home team. Or date differences! Maybe HIST dates are one day off from BRAS? Or... Let me debug: count 2014 in each source: BRAS 2014: 380, HIST 2014: 380, BRF 2014: 281. 380+380 = 760 potential, dedup → if all matched: 380 (+ BRF extras). Got 574. So significant mismatch — around 186 mismatches. Also 2013: BRAS 380 + HIST 380 = 760 → got 418?? That's less than 760 — wait 418 < 760, dedupe removed ~342 — that means most DID match (760 - 342 = 418)... hmm inconsistent.\n\nWait no: 2013 has no BRF (BRF starts 2014). BRAS 2013: 380, HIST 2013: 380. If they matched perfectly, dedupe → 380. Got 418 — so 38 didn't match. Interesting — 38 = one round? Maybe HIST has different dates for some matches (e.g., BRAS datetime is the *scheduled* date vs HIST the *actual* date, or timezone). Hmm.\n\n2014: BRAS 380 + HIST 380 + BRF 281 = 1441 max. Got 574. If BRAS↔HIST mostly matched (like 2013, ~38 unmatched): 380 + 38 + BRF overlap... BRF 2014 has 281 Serie A rows — 2014 Serie A had 380 matches; BRF incomplete. If BRF's 281 mostly overlap BRAS/HIST... Got 574 — let me think: unique = BRAS∪HIST∪BRF. If BRAS∪HIST ≈ 418 (like 2013) and BRF adds 156 new → 574. Hmm BRF adding 156 new matches in 2014? That seems odd — unless date/team normalization differs for BRF (e.g., BRF dates or names differ so same matches don't dedupe).\n\nRather than speculate, debug it: for 2014, find near-miss pairs (same teams, dates within 3 days) between sources. Also 2013 between BRAS and HIST.\n\nAlso check BRF 2021 Serie A internal dupes (491 rows vs 380 expected — the earlier dup count output didn't print because the script died before. And 2021 dedup count 775! That's way over 380. BRAS 2021: 380, HIST ends 2019. So 2021 = BRAS 380 + BRF 491 → deduped 775?? That means almost NO overlap matched — 380+491=871, deduped 775 → only 96 matched. Something's wrong with matching between BRAS and BRF for 2021. Maybe BRF 2021 dates are shifted, or BRF has duplicate rows with same key but I dedupe on (date, home, away) — internal dupes should collapse. 491 with internal dupes → unique BRF keys maybe ~380+? Hmm wait — maybe BRF 2021 Serie A includes BOTH the regular 380 AND something else. Let me look at actual 2021 BRF rows.\n\nLet me debug all of this concretely.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c680eaa001IeQfz5U6OQQ78U","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c67cc9b001FZkScJ19pCp2cp"}}
