{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788256765675,"sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b524490a76456cdf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import defaultdict, Counter\n\ndef rows(p):\n    with open(p, encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\ndef deacc(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\nbra = rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\ncupa = rows('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\nlib = rows('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nbf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nhist = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\n\n# All distinct raw team strings\nraw = Counter()\nfor r in bra: raw[r['home_team']]+=1; raw[r['away_team']]+=1\nfor r in cupa: raw[r['home_team']]+=1; raw[r['away_team']]+=1\nfor r in lib: raw[r['home_team']]+=1; raw[r['away_team']]+=1\nfor r in bf: raw[r['home']]+=1; raw[r['away']]+=1\nfor r in hist: raw[r['Equipe_mandante']]+=1; raw[r['Equipe_visitante']]+=1\nprint(\"total distinct raw team strings:\", len(raw))\n\n# base = accent-stripped lowercase, UF-suffix stripped\nUF = {'AC','AL','AP','AM','BA','CE','DF','ES','GO','MA','MT','MS','MG','PA','PB','PR','PE','PI','RJ','RN','RS','RO','RR','SC','SP','SE','TO'}\ndef base_of(name):\n    s = deacc(name).lower().replace('.', ' ')\n    s = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', s).strip()\n    m = re.search(r'^(.*?)[\\s]*[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', s)\n    if m and m.group(2).upper() in UF:\n        return m.group(1).strip(), m.group(2).upper()\n    return s, None\n\nbase2uf = defaultdict(set)\nuf_examples = defaultdict(dict)\nfor name in raw:\n    b, uf = base_of(name)\n    if uf:\n        base2uf[b].add(uf)\n        uf_examples[b].setdefault(uf, name)\n# bases with multiple UFs -> ambiguous\namb = {b: ufs for b, ufs in base2uf.items() if len(ufs) > 1}\nprint(\"\\nambiguous bases (multiple UFs):\")\nfor b, ufs in sorted(amb.items()):\n    print(f\"  '{b}': {sorted(ufs)} e.g. {[uf_examples[b][u] for u in sorted(ufs)][:4]}\")\n\n# how often do bases appear WITHOUT any uf suffix (bare)?\nbare = defaultdict(int)\nfor name, n in raw.items():\n    b, uf = base_of(name)\n    if uf is None:\n        bare[b] += n\nprint(\"\\ntop bare (no-UF) names:\", sorted(bare.items(), key=lambda x:-x[1])[:20])\nEOF"},"output":"total distinct raw team strings: 725\n\nambiguous bases (multiple UFs):\n  'america': ['MG', 'RN'] e.g. ['America-MG', 'América - RN']\n  'atletico': ['AC', 'BA', 'ES', 'GO', 'MG', 'PR'] e.g. ['Atlético - AC', 'Atlético - BA', 'Atletico - ES', 'Atletico-GO']\n  'botafogo': ['PB', 'RJ'] e.g. ['Botafogo - PB', 'Botafogo-RJ']\n  'bragantino': ['PA', 'SP'] e.g. ['Bragantino - PA', 'Bragantino - SP']\n  'comercial': ['MS', 'PI'] e.g. ['Comercial - MS', 'Comercial - PI']\n  'flamengo': ['PI', 'RJ'] e.g. ['Flamengo - PI', 'Flamengo-RJ']\n  'guarani': ['CE', 'SP'] e.g. ['Guarani - CE', 'Guarani - SP']\n  'internacional': ['RS', 'SC'] e.g. ['Internacional-RS', 'Internacional - SC']\n  'juventude': ['MA', 'RS'] e.g. ['Juventude - MA', 'Juventude-RS']\n  'nautico': ['PE', 'RR'] e.g. ['Nautico-PE', 'Nautico - RR']\n  'operario': ['MS', 'MT', 'PR'] e.g. ['Operário - MS', 'Operário - MT', 'Operario - PR']\n  'rio branco': ['AC', 'ES'] e.g. ['Rio Branco - AC', 'Rio Branco - ES']\n  'santa cruz': ['PE', 'RN', 'RS'] e.g. ['Santa Cruz-PE', 'Santa Cruz - RN', 'Santa Cruz - RS']\n  'santos': ['AP', 'SP'] e.g. ['Santos - AP', 'Santos-SP']\n  'sao raimundo': ['PA', 'RR'] e.g. ['São Raimundo - PA', 'São Raimundo - RR']\n  'ypiranga': ['AP', 'RS'] e.g. ['Ypiranga - AP', 'Ypiranga - RS']\n\ntop bare (no-UF) names: [('flamengo', 1168), ('cruzeiro', 1139), ('sao paulo', 1136), ('santos', 1136), ('gremio', 1119), ('fluminense', 1108), ('corinthians', 1098), ('palmeiras', 1083), ('internacional', 1073), ('goias', 880), ('coritiba', 868), ('vitoria', 767), ('ponte preta', 766), ('figueirense', 766), ('chapecoense', 629), ('avai', 624), ('ceara', 569), ('vasco', 558), ('parana', 543), ('criciuma', 527)]\n","metadata":{"output":"total distinct raw team strings: 725\n\nambiguous bases (multiple UFs):\n  'america': ['MG', 'RN'] e.g. ['America-MG', 'América - RN']\n  'atletico': ['AC', 'BA', 'ES', 'GO', 'MG', 'PR'] e.g. ['Atlético - AC', 'Atlético - BA', 'Atletico - ES', 'Atletico-GO']\n  'botafogo': ['PB', 'RJ'] e.g. ['Botafogo - PB', 'Botafogo-RJ']\n  'bragantino': ['PA', 'SP'] e.g. ['Bragantino - PA', 'Bragantino - SP']\n  'comercial': ['MS', 'PI'] e.g. ['Comercial - MS', 'Comercial - PI']\n  'flamengo': ['PI', 'RJ'] e.g. ['Flamengo - PI', 'Flamengo-RJ']\n  'guarani': ['CE', 'SP'] e.g. ['Guarani - CE', 'Guarani - SP']\n  'internacional': ['RS', 'SC'] e.g. ['Internacional-RS', 'Internacional - SC']\n  'juventude': ['MA', 'RS'] e.g. ['Juventude - MA', 'Juventude-RS']\n  'nautico': ['PE', 'RR'] e.g. ['Nautico-PE', 'Nautico - RR']\n  'operario': ['MS', 'MT', 'PR'] e.g. ['Operário - MS', 'Operário - MT', 'Operario - PR']\n  'rio branco': ['AC', 'ES'] e.g. ['Rio Branco - AC', 'Rio Branco - ES']\n  'santa cruz': ['PE', 'RN', 'RS'] e.g. ['Santa Cruz-PE', 'Santa Cruz - RN', 'Santa Cruz - RS']\n  'santos': ['AP', 'SP'] e.g. ['Santos - AP', 'Santos-SP']\n  'sao raimundo': ['PA', 'RR'] e.g. ['São Raimundo - PA', 'São Raimundo - RR']\n  'ypiranga': ['AP', 'RS'] e.g. ['Ypiranga - AP', 'Ypiranga - RS']\n\ntop bare (no-UF) names: [('flamengo', 1168), ('cruzeiro', 1139), ('sao paulo', 1136), ('santos', 1136), ('gremio', 1119), ('fluminense', 1108), ('corinthians', 1098), ('palmeiras', 1083), ('internacional', 1073), ('goias', 880), ('coritiba', 868), ('vitoria', 767), ('ponte preta', 766), ('figueirense', 766), ('chapecoense', 629), ('avai', 624), ('ceara', 569), ('vasco', 558), ('parana', 543), ('criciuma', 527)]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import defaultdict, Counter\n\ndef rows(p):\n    with open(p, encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\ndef deacc(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\nbra = rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\ncupa = rows('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\nlib = rows('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nbf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nhist = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\n\n# All distinct raw team strings\nraw = Counter()\nfor r in bra: raw[r['home_team']]+=1; raw[r['away_team']]+=1\nfor r in cupa: raw[r['home_team']]+=1; raw[r['away_team']]+=1\nfor r in lib: raw[r['home_team']]+=1; raw[r['away_team']]+=1\nfor r in bf: raw[r['home']]+=1; raw[r['away']]+=1\nfor r in hist: raw[r['Equipe_mandante']]+=1; raw[r['Equipe_visitante']]+=1\nprint(\"total distinct raw team strings:\", len(raw))\n\n# base = accent-stripped lowercase, UF-suffix stripped\nUF = {'AC','AL','AP','AM','BA','CE','DF','ES','GO','MA','MT','MS','MG','PA','PB','PR','PE','PI','RJ','RN','RS','RO','RR','SC','SP','SE','TO'}\ndef base_of(name):\n    s = deacc(name).lower().replace('.', ' ')\n    s = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', s).strip()\n    m = re.search(r'^(.*?)[\\s]*[-–]\\s*([a-z]{2})$', s)\n    if m and m.group(2).upper() in UF:\n        return m.group(1).strip(), m.group(2).upper()\n    return s, None\n\nbase2uf = defaultdict(set)\nuf_examples = defaultdict(dict)\nfor name in raw:\n    b, uf = base_of(name)\n    if uf:\n        base2uf[b].add(uf)\n        uf_examples[b].setdefault(uf, name)\n# bases with multiple UFs -> ambiguous\namb = {b: ufs for b, ufs in base2uf.items() if len(ufs) > 1}\nprint(\"\\nambiguous bases (multiple UFs):\")\nfor b, ufs in sorted(amb.items()):\n    print(f\"  '{b}': {sorted(ufs)} e.g. {[uf_examples[b][u] for u in sorted(ufs)][:4]}\")\n\n# how often do bases appear WITHOUT any uf suffix (bare)?\nbare = defaultdict(int)\nfor name, n in raw.items():\n    b, uf = base_of(name)\n    if uf is None:\n        bare[b] += n\nprint(\"\\ntop bare (no-UF) names:\", sorted(bare.items(), key=lambda x:-x[1])[:20])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788256765669,"end":1788256765674}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Found it! The mystery unmatched keys all involve `'atletico'` vs `'athletico'` — without the \"-PR\" suffix! Looking at unmatched bras keys: `('2013-09-22', 'atletico', 'ponte preta')` and unmatched hist: `('2013-09-22', 'athletico', 'ponte preta')` — SAME date, same opponent, but one says \"atletico\" and other \"athletico\".\n\nWhy is the suffix missing? Because in BRAS 2013 the team is probably \"Atletico-MG\"? No wait — if it were Atletico-MG, norm → \"atletico mg\" ≠ \"atletico\". The bare \"atletico\" means the raw name was exactly \"Atletico-PR\" → strip \"-pr\" → \"atletico\"?? No — stripping \"-PR\" from \"Atletico-PR\" gives \"atletico\", not \"atletico pr\"!\n\nMy norm function strips the UF suffix entirely — so \"Atletico-PR\" → \"atletico\" and \"Atlético-PR\" → \"atletico\". But then how did the common 342 match? Because most BRAS names like \"Palmeiras-SP\" → \"palmeiras\" match HIST \"Palmeiras\" → \"palmeiras\". ✓.\n\nThe issue: my ALIAS maps 'athletico pr' → 'atletico pr', but after suffix stripping the keys are 'athletico' vs 'atletico' — the alias never fires! I need alias on the post-strip form: 'athletico' → 'atletico'. But wait — 'atletico' alone is ambiguous (Atletico-MG? Atletico-PR? Atletico-GO?). In 2013 BRAS, which \"Atletico\" is it? BRAS 2013 has \"Atletico-MG\" AND \"Atletico-PR\". Both would normalize to \"atletico\"!! COLLISION! Let me check: BRAS 2013 teams — \"Atletico-MG\", \"Atletico-PR\" both present → norm both → \"atletico\". That's a huge bug: two different clubs collapse to one key!\n\nAlso \"Atletico-GO\" in 2012/2020+. So stripping UF creates collisions between Atlético-MG / Atlético-PR / Atlético-GO.\n\nAnd in HIST, teams are \"Atlético-MG\" AND \"Athletico-PR\" (accented, Athletico for PR) → norm → \"atletico\" vs \"athletico\" — distinct. But BRAS has BOTH as \"atletico\" → collision!\n\nSo the right canonical form must KEEP the differentiating part. The UF suffix is actually what disambiguates Atlético-MG from Atlético-PR! \"América-MG\" vs \"América-RN\" likewise!\n\nNew approach: canonical key = name WITHOUT generic club-designator words but WITH disambiguation. Options:\n\n**Option A: keep the state suffix in the canonical key.** \"Palmeiras-SP\" → key \"palmeiras sp\"; HIST \"Palmeiras\" → key \"palmeiras\"... then they don't match. Bad — unless we build the registry from all variants and unify variants observed to refer to same club. But how do we know \"Palmeiras\" (HIST, no suffix) is Palmeiras-SP and not some other Palmeiras? Context: within a league season, team sets are known... too clever.\n\n**Option B: canonical key strips UF, but collisions get disambiguated via per-file context.** Complex.\n\n**Option C: use a curated canonical mapping.** The set of teams is finite and known. Build registry with base names + disambiguation for collisions:\n- For most teams, base name (UF-stripped) is unique → key = base (\"palmeiras\").\n- For collision bases (atletico, america, sport?, vitoria?, internacional is unique...), the UF is REQUIRED to disambiguate: key = base + ' ' + uf (\"atletico pr\", \"atletico mg\", \"atletico go\").\n\nSo the rule: strip UF by default, BUT keep it when the base would be ambiguous. Two-phase build:\n1. Normalize every raw team string to (base, uf) where uf = trailing UF code if present.\n2. Collect all bases across the dataset. A base is \"ambiguous\" if it maps to multiple UFs (atletico: MG, PR, GO; america: MG, RN; etc.).\n3. Canonical key = base if unambiguous base, else base+uf.\n\nBut then \"Atletico-MG\" (BRAS) → \"atletico mg\" and HIST \"Atlético-MG\" → \"atletico mg\" ✓ match. BRAS \"Atletico-PR\" → \"atletico pr\", HIST \"Athletico-PR\" → \"athletico pr\" — alias 'athletico pr' → 'atletico pr' fixes. BRAS \"Atletico-GO\" → \"atletico go\", HIST \"Atlético-GO\" → \"atletico go\" ✓.\n\nWhat about HIST \"Athletico-PR\" in years where it's spelled... wait HIST uses \"Athletico-PR\" only from 2019 (renamed); earlier \"Atlético-PR\". Fine.\n\nBut what about a file where Atlético-PR appears WITHOUT suffix, e.g. Libertadores \"Athletico\" (saw in LIB samples: 'Athletico'!). LIB team \"Athletico\" → base \"athletico\", no UF → what's it? Athletico-PR presumably (only Brazilian Athletico in Libertadores). Similarly LIB \"América-MG\" has suffix. Hmm \"Athletico\" bare: base 'athletico' — ambiguous-base set contains 'atletico' (via alias) — bare 'athletico' with no UF... resolve to 'atletico pr'? Since Athletico-PR is the only one of the atletico family commonly in Libertadores. But Atletico-MG and Atletico-GO have also played Libertadores (Atlético-MG won it 2013!). Do they appear bare as \"Atlético\"? Possibly! Ugh.\n\nLet me check LIB team list for all atletico/america variants. Also BRF team names (which have no UF mostly — \"4 de Julho EC\", \"Aguia Negra-MS\"). BRF Serie A teams for atletico: e.g. \"Atletico Mineiro\"? Let me check BRF team strings for Serie A/B teams — they might use FULL names like \"Atletico Mineiro\", \"Atletico Goianiense\", \"Athletico Paranaense\"! That would resolve ambiguity naturally: \"atletico mineiro\" → base \"atletico mineiro\". Then BRF \"atletico mineiro\" vs BRAS \"Atletico-MG\" → \"atletico mg\" — DON'T match! Need alias: \"atletico mineiro\" → \"atletico mg\", \"atletico goianiense\"/\"atletico go\" → \"atletico go\", \"atletico paranaense\"/\"athletico paranaense\" → \"atletico pr\", \"vasco da gama\" → \"vasco\", \"atletico tubarao\"? etc.\n\nOK this is the crux of the \"team name normalization\" challenge the spec warns about. My plan:\n\n1. **Variant extraction**: from every raw team string, compute `base_candidate` (UF-stripped, accent-stripped, punctuation-removed, club-designator words like 'ec','fc','ac'?? removed — careful, check data) and `uf` (the stripped suffix, if any).\n\n2. **Curated alias table** (manual, verified against data) mapping full names to canonical keys:\n   - 'atletico mineiro' → 'atletico mg'\n   - 'atletico goianiense' → 'atletico go'\n   - 'atletico paranaense' / 'athletico paranaense' → 'atletico pr'\n   - 'athletico' → 'atletico pr' (Libertadores bare form — VERIFY from data that bare 'athletico'/'atletico' rows in LIB are really PR)\n   - 'vasco da gama' → 'vasco'\n   - 'gremio foot ball porto alegrense'? → 'gremio'\n   - 'botafogo de futebol e regatas'? → 'botafogo'\n   - 'clube de regatas do flamengo'? → 'flamengo'\n   - 'sao paulo fc'? 'sao paulo'\n   - 'sport club corinthians paulista' → 'corinthians'\n   - 'sport recife' → 'sport' (Sport-PE → 'sport')\n   - 'fortaleza esporte clube'? etc.\n   - 'guarani fc'? → 'guarani'\n   - 'cruzeiro esporte clube' → 'cruzeiro'\n   - 'ponte preta' → 'ponte preta' fine\n   - 'vila nova fc'? 'vila nova'\n   - 'ceara sporting club'? 'ceara'\n   \n   Instead of enumerating every possibility blindly, I should EXTRACT the actual team strings from the data (union of all 6 files) and hand-curate. The number of distinct teams is maybe ~300 across files (many small clubs in Copa/BRF Serie B/C). For dedupe correctness only the BIG clubs matter (the overlapping Serie A/Copa files). For search, a good general algorithm + aliases for the big clubs suffices.\n\n3. **Ambiguity rule**: base names appearing with multiple UFs get key = base+uf. Deterministic from data at load time.\n\nLet me now enumerate ALL distinct team strings across files to see the real scale, then design precisely. Let me also check BRF Serie A team names, LIB atletico variants, and Copa do Brasil round-8 seasons.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c68ab920016NGl4qjuwVp1wa","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c682ff8001PDGTfALYzb8L14"}}
