c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\nbra = rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\ncupa = rows('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\nlib = rows('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nbf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nhist = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\n\ndef show(label, names, pred):\n    print(f\"{label}: {sorted({n for n in names if pred(deacc(n).lower())})}\")\n\nallnames = set()\nfor r in bra: allnames |= {r['home_team'], r['away_team']}\nshow(\"BRAS atletico/vasco-ish\", allnames, lambda s: 'atlet' in s or 'vasco' in s or 'paranaense' in s or 'mineiro' in s)\n\nallnames_c = set()\nfor r in cupa: allnames_c |= {r['home_team'], r['away_team']}\nshow(\"COPA big club spellings\", allnames_c, lambda s: any(k in s for k in ['corinthians','flamengo','palmeiras','vasco','atlet','mineiro','paranaense','gremio','cruzeiro','santos','paulista']))\n\nallnames_l = set()\nfor r in lib: allnames_l |= {r['home_team'], r['away_team']}\nshow(\"LIB atletico/athletico/braz big\", allnames_l, lambda s: any(k in s for k in ['atlet','athlet','mineiro','paranaense','vasco','gremio','flamengo','palmeiras','santos','paulista','cruzeiro','corinthians','internacional','chapecoense','fortaleza','ceara','avai','bahia','goias','coritiba','fluminense','botafogo','sport']))\n\nallnames_b = set()\nfor r in bf: allnames_b |= {r['home'], r['away']}\nshow(\"BRF atletico variants\", allnames_b, lambda s: 'atlet' in s or 'paranaense' in s or 'mineiro' in s or 'goianiense' in s)\nshow(\"BRF big clubs\", allnames_b, lambda s: any(k in s for k in ['flamengo','palmeiras','corinthians','vasco','gremio fb','cruzeiro','sao paulo','santos fc','fluminense','botafogo','internacional','sport','fortaleza','ceara','bahia de','bahia','vitoria','goias','coritiba','avai','chapecoense','criciuma','ponte preta','atletico go','athletico','parana clube','guarani','figueirense','america mg','america rn','cuiaba','juventude','nautico','santa cruz','bragantino','red bull']))\nprint(\"BRF 'bahia' matches:\", [n for n in allnames_b if 'bahia' in deacc(n).lower()])\nprint(\"BRF 'sport':\", [n for n in allnames_b if deacc(n).lower().startswith('sport')][:6])\nprint(\"BRF 'santos':\", [n for n in allnames_b if deacc(n).lower().startswith('santos')][:6])\n\nallnames_h = set()\nfor r in hist: allnames_h |= {r['Equipe_mandante'], r['Equipe_visitante']}\nshow(\"HIST atletico/vasco\", allnames_h, lambda s: 'atlet' in s or 'vasco' in s)\n\n# Copa do Brasil: which seasons have round 8? (final)\nprint(\"\\nCOPA round 8 by season:\", sorted(Counter(r['season'] for r in cupa if r['round']=='8').items()))\nprint(\"COPA round 7 by season:\", sorted(Counter(r['season'] for r in cupa if r['round']=='7').items()))\n# LIB bare atletico/athletico rows\nfor r in lib:\n    nm = deacc(r['home_team']).lower()\n    if nm in ('atletico','athletico'):\n        print(\"LIB bare:\", r['home_team'], r['season'], r['stage'])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788256790399,"end":1788256790404}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I see the real landscape:\n\n**Ambiguous bases** (UF needed for disambiguation): atletico (AC, BA, ES, GO, MG, PR!), america (MG, RN), botafogo (PB, RJ), bragantino (PA, SP), comercial, flamengo (PI, RJ!), guarani (CE, SP), internacional (RS, SC), juventude, nautico, operario, rio branco, santa cruz, santos (AP, SP!), sao raimundo, ypiranga.\n\nNote \"santos - AP\" and \"flamengo - PI\" are tiny clubs (Santos-AP, Flamengo-PI) that appear in Copa do Brasil early rounds. The BIG Santos (SP) appears bare \"Santos\" 1136 times + \"Santos-SP\". So for Santos: bare = Santos-SP (the giant); \"Santos - AP\" is the minnow.\n\n**The design that handles all this cleanly:**\n\nCanonical key = `base` if base is unambiguous, else `base + ' ' + uf`. And for BARE occurrences of an ambiguous base (e.g., bare \"Santos\" 1136 times, bare \"Atletico\"?) — we need to resolve them. Data-driven resolution:\n\nFor each ambiguous base, look at bare usage counts: bare \"santos\" 1136 → dominant club is Santos-SP. If exactly one UF variant is \"major\" (e.g., appears in Serie A seasons with many matches), map bare → that variant. That's getting heuristic. Simpler deterministic rule: **for an ambiguous base, bare form maps to the UF-variant with the most total occurrences in the whole dataset** (Santos-SP dominates Santos-AP by 1136+ vs few; Flamengo-RJ dominates Flamengo-PI; Botafogo-RJ dominates Botafogo-PB; America? América-MG vs América-RN — both are real clubs with decent history. América-MG played Série A many seasons; América-RN also (2014-2016 Série A?). Counts decide. It's data-driven and deterministic; ties broken alphabetically. For atletico bare — e.g., LIB \"Athletico\" bare and maybe \"Atlético\" bare — count-based could misassign (Atletico-MG has more total matches than Atletico-PR probably, so bare \"Atlético\" in Libertadores (if meaning MG) fine, but bare \"Athletico\" (the renamed PR spelling!) → deacc → \"atletico\" → would map to MG — WRONG for LIB rows after 2019!\n\nBetter: **spelling-aware resolution**: keep the pre-alias raw base ('athletico' vs 'atletico') — map 'athletico' → atletico pr always (unique rename), and bare 'atletico' → count-dominant atletico variant (MG). Let me verify: in LIB, is bare \"Atlético\" = Atlético-MG (2013-2017 era, e.g. \"Atlético\" vs \"Atletico Nacional\"?) and bare \"Athletico\" = Athletico-PR (2019+)? Check LIB raw names containing atletico/athletico. Also BRF names for these clubs. Let me check what BRF calls them (probably \"Atletico Mineiro\"/\"Athletico Paranaense\"/\"Atletico Goianiense\" full names — check). And what HIST calls them: \"Atlético-MG\"/\"Athletico-PR\"/\"Atlético-GO\".\n\nAlso Copa file full names like \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"? Spec mentions it. Let me grep Copa/BRF for the big clubs' raw strings to build the alias table.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0