ão Paulo\", \"Athletico-PR\"→\"Athletico Paranaense\"? Keep it simple: display = deacc'd? NO — spec requires UTF-8 handling, so display accented forms. I'll pick the most frequent raw variant, then if it has a trailing UF, strip it for display. E.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\" → \"Palmeiras\"; \"Atlético-MG\" → \"Atlético-MG\"?? stripping gives \"Atlético\" — ambiguous display! For ambiguous-base keys, KEEP the UF in display: \"Atlético-MG\", \"América-RN\", \"Botafogo-PB\", \"Internacional-SC\" etc. And for alias-derived keys like 'atletico pr' display \"Athletico-PR\" (most frequent suffixed raw). Good: display rule = most-frequent raw variant (ties → longest/most-informative), but never strip UF if key is ambiguous-base. Hmm, simplest robust: if key endswith uf → display = f\"{BaseTitle}-{UF}\" using the most frequent raw's casing? I'll implement: for each key, collect raw variants; display = the raw variant with the highest count; if that variant lacks accents but another (same count-ish) has, prefer accented. Simpler: prefer the raw variant with max (count, has_accent). For bare keys like 'palmeiras', raws: \"Palmeiras-SP\"(n), \"Palmeiras\"(m) — display: strip UF from the winner → \"Palmeiras\". I'll implement display = winner raw with UF-suffix stripped ONLY when key is unambiguous-bare. Otherwise keep full.\n\nThis is getting complex but it IS the core challenge of the task. I'll implement carefully in `normalize.py` with a TeamRegistry class and unit tests for the tricky pairs.\n\n**Verify dedupe target numbers**: After canonicalization, per-season Série A dedup counts should be:\n- 2003-2005: 552/552/462 (HIST only)\n- 2006-2011: 380\n- 2012-2019: 380 (BRAS+HIST dedupe)\n- 2020-2022: 380 (BRAS+BRF... BRF 2020 has only 264 → BRAS 380 dominates; BRF adds none new? If BRF 2020 ⊂ BRAS 2020 → 380)\n- 2023: 377 (BRF only)\n- 2014-2019 BRF extras: BRF Serie A 2014 281 rows — should all overlap BRAS/HIST 380 → no new. So target: all seasons ≤ 380 (except 2003-2005 and 2023).\n\nBRF 2021 491 rows → internal dupes? If BRF has internal duplicate (date, home, away) rows, they collapse. If BRF 2021 contains matches with same teams but different dates that AREN'T in BRAS (e.g., BRF lists both \"Flamengo 2-1 Palmeiras 2021-09-08\" AND BRAS has same) — dedupe key catches. If dates differ between sources for same fixture (postponed/rescheduled), we'd get phantom extra matches per season. My earlier broken run got 2021: 775 — because 'atletico' collision etc. made keys differ... no wait collision makes MORE matching not less... whatever — recompute with correct canonicalization and check per-season counts ≈ 380. If some seasons have e.g. 381-390, investigate date mismatches; possibly dedupe on (season, home, away) for Serie A when round-ish consistent? NO — two-leg competitions (copa) legitimately have same-season same-teams twice. For Serie A league each pair meets twice (home+away) — key (season, home, away) appears exactly twice legitimately! So date-based dedupe is right; but a rescheduled match with different recorded dates in two sources would double-count. Check final counts; if slightly over 380, consider (date±1, home, away) fuzzy? Let me first compute exact numbers with the full canonicalization, then decide.\n\nAlso **standings correctness**: with dedupe → 2019: Flamengo 90pts/28W/6D/4L (spec-stated truth), Santos 74, Palmeiras 74. If computed standings match → canonicalization+dedupe validated end-to-end.\n\n**FIFA club names**: check for Flamengo/São Paulo/Palmeiras etc. Earlier grep missed Flamengo... let me verify. Also FIFA \"Santos\" vs \"Santos Laguna\" — club filter must use exact normalized equality (not substring) to avoid that. And check whether FIFA has Brazilian Série A clubs at all: Grêmio 20, Fluminense 20, Santos 20, Internacional 20, Botafogo 20, Bahia 20, Atlético Paranaense 20, Atlético Mineiro 20, Cruzeiro 20... Flamengo missing?? Suspicious. Check.\n\nLet me now write a comprehensive prototype implementing the full canonicalization and validate: dedupe counts per season, 2019+2020 standings, FIFA clubs. Then I'll write the real package files.\n\nActually — time to write the REAL code now (the design is validated enough); I'll iterate on it via tests. Write:\n\n1. `brsoccer/normalize.py` — canonicalization + registry\n2. `brsoccer/dates.py`\n3. `brsoccer/models.py`\n4. `brsoccer/data.py`\n5. `brsoccer/queries.py`\n6. `brsoccer/formatting.py`\n7. `brsoccer/mcp_server.py`\n8. `server.py`\n9. `tests/*`\n10. `pyproject.toml`, `requirements.txt`, `pytest.ini`\n\nLet me check FIFA clubs for Flamengo first (one more data check), then write code.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c6a0dba001jat5I5hL9eIiDq","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c6928ae001iNc9jwUosmsvc5"}}
