'2020-08-16', 2, 1)]\n      reverse pair rows: [('BR-Football-Dataset.csv', '2020-11-20', 4, 0)]\n\n2021: pairs=418 reversed-dupes=0\n\n2022: pairs=418 reversed-dupes=0\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom brsoccer.data import _raw_rows, find_data_dir\nfrom brsoccer.normalize import TeamRegistry\n\nraw = _raw_rows(find_data_dir())\nreg = TeamRegistry()\nfor r in raw:\n    reg.ingest(r['home_raw']); reg.ingest(r['away_raw'])\nreg.finalize()\n\ndef fixed_season(r):\n    if r['source']=='BR-Football-Dataset.csv' and r['competition'] in ('serie_a','serie_b','serie_c'):\n        d = r['date']\n        if d and d.month <= 2:\n            return d.year - 1\n    return r['season']\n\nfor season in (2015, 2020, 2021, 2022):\n    buckets = defaultdict(list)\n    for r in raw:\n        if r['competition']!='serie_a': continue\n        s = fixed_season(r)\n        if s != season: continue\n        buckets[(reg.key_of(r['home_raw']), reg.key_of(r['away_raw']))].append(r)\n    # reversed-pair detection: (A,B) and (B,A) same date/score\n    keys = set(buckets)\n    reversed_hits = []\n    for (h, a) in keys:\n        if (a, h) in keys and h < a:\n            for r1 in buckets[(h, a)]:\n                for r2 in buckets[(a, h)]:\n                    if r1['date'] == r2['date'] and (r1['home_goal'], r1['away_goal']) == (r2['away_goal'], r2['home_goal']) and r1['home_goal'] is not None:\n                        reversed_hits.append(((h,a), r1['date'], r1['home_goal'], r1['away_goal'], r1['source'], r2['source']))\n    print(f\"\\n{season}: pairs={len(keys)} reversed-dupes={len(reversed_hits)}\")\n    for x in reversed_hits[:5]: print(\"   REVERSED:\", x)\n    # what sources contribute per pair for extras in 2020\n    if season in (2020,):\n        # which pairs are NOT in BRAS?\n        bras_pairs = {(reg.key_of(r['home_raw']), reg.key_of(r['away_raw'])) for r in raw if r['competition']=='serie_a' and r['source']=='Brasileirao_Matches.csv' and r['season']==season}\n        extra = keys - bras_pairs\n        print(f\"  extra pairs not in BRAS: {len(extra)}\")\n        for (h,a) in list(extra)[:10]:\n            rows = buckets[(h,a)]\n            print(\"   EXTRA:\", h, a, [(r['source'], str(r['date']), r['home_goal'], r['away_goal']) for r in rows])\n            # is the reverse in bras?\n            rev = (a, h)\n            print(\"      reverse pair rows:\", [(r['source'], str(r['date']), r['home_goal'], r['away_goal']) for r in buckets.get(rev, [])][:3])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788257396481,"end":1788257396490}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Great diagnosis. Results:\n\n**serie_a**: bucket by (season, home, away) works beautifully: agree=4049, conflict=12 (score conflicts between sources — keep priority). Unique ordered pairs per season: 2006-2019: 380 ✓✓; 2020-2022: 418 (extra 38 pairs!). Hmm — 418 = 380 + 38. What are the extra 38 ordered pairs in 2020? Probably the season-fix: BRF Jan/Feb 2021 rows → season 2020. But BRAS 2020 might have those same fixtures... 418 unique pairs with multi-buckets agreeing... The extra 38: maybe BRF 2020 rows that BRAS lacks — BRF 2020 Serie A had 264 rows only. Hmm 2020: BRAS 380 pairs + BRF-shifted rows. If BRF's Feb-2021 rows (2020 tail) include pairs that BRAS 2020 also has → bucket merge → still 380 total. Got 418 → 38 pairs extra. Which? Possibly pairs where BRF season-fix put rows in 2020 that actually belong elsewhere, OR BRAS 2020 records a fixture that BRF records in \"2020\" from Jan/Feb... hmm wait I bet the 38 extra pairs are the 2020-season matches that BRAS dated in Jan/Feb 2021 but BRF ALSO dated Jan/Feb 2021 — no that would merge...\n\nWait — maybe the issue is reversed: BRAS season column for the pandemic season: does BRAS call the Jan/Feb 2021 matches \"2020\"? BRAS season column is explicit ✓. HIST none. So 2020 pairs = union(BRAS-2020 pairs, BRF rows assigned 2020). BRAS 2020: 380. BRF 2020: rows dated 2020-08..2020-12 (264-ish) + rows dated 2021-01/02 (shifted). If BRF contains 38 ordered pairs NOT in BRAS-2020... e.g., BRF might record BOTH legs of some pairs with different... no, ordered pairs. Hmm — OR the 38 extra are pairs where BRAS says home=A but BRF says home=B (reversed venue) for the same fixture!! With pandemic neutral venues?? Or data errors. Let me diagnose the 2020 extras concretely.\n\nAlso 2015: 381 pairs (one extra) and 2009: 379 (one missing — data hole, fine).\n\n**serie_b**: buckets multi=0 — BRF is the only source, no internal dupes (post season-fix... wait did the fix move serie_b Jan/Feb rows? 2021 serie_b: 379 — hmm 2020 serie_b: 369 — missing 11, fine-ish, data holes).\n\n**serie_c**: conflict=55 — ordered pairs repeat WITHIN BRF (final-phase rematches with different scores — legit per my earlier concern) — so serie_c must use date-based dedupe, NOT pair-collapse. The 6 \"agree\" are probably true dupes. Use fuzzy date dedupe for serie_c.\n\n**copa**: BRF 1123 rows; 377 exact + 372 fuzzy(±1d) matched vs COPA file; 374 unmatched. The unmatched: BRF 2022-2023 (no COPA file coverage: 117+116=233 ✓) + 141 others (2014-2021 BRF rows not matching COPA file — small-club spelling mismatches or real date shifts >1 day, or BRF listing matches the COPA file lacks). 374-233=141. Hmm. Those 141 BRF-only rows could be: (a) same-match different-date (>1 day off), (b) different team spellings (small clubs), (c) genuinely different matches (COPA file incomplete for early rounds?). COPA file 2015 has 158 vs BRF 2015 139 — COPA has MORE per season than BRF for 2014-2016; BRF has more 2017+ (120 vs 105-111). So both files are incomplete in different ways — the union is the honest dataset. Dupes inflate per-season counts slightly (2015: 158+139=297 rows → after exact+fuzzy dedupe ~158 + unmatched-BRF ~... ). For a knockout cup, inflated match lists are less harmful (no standings). I'll do exact + ±1day fuzzy dedupe (same teams only, regardless of score? no — same teams AND (same score or one side missing score)). 372 fuzzy currently counted regardless of score — let me require score agreement OR one is None, else treat as separate (two-legged ties same teams within a few days? Two legs are usually 1-2 weeks apart, not ≤1 day. Safe.)\n\nSo final dedupe design:\n- **serie_a, serie_b**: collapse on (season, home, away) — 1 row per ordered pair per season (priority source wins conflicts; merge stats/venue/kickoff from dupes). 2009: 379 (hole in data), 2015: 381 (one extra pair — investigate: likely BRF pair where BRAS has reversed home/away or a genuinely phantom row. 381 won't corrupt standings materially (one team gets +1 match). Actually let me check the 2015 extra and the 2020 extra-38 — if they're reversed-venue duplicates I can catch them: for each season, check if any TWO buckets are (A,B) and (B,A) with same date & same score → same match recorded with swapped venue → merge keeping BRAS's version. Let me diagnose.)\n- **serie_c, copa_do_brasil, libertadores**: exact (date, home, away) key + fuzzy pass merging (same comp+season+teams, |Δdate|≤1, score-agree-or-missing).\n\nLet me diagnose the 2020 (418-380=38) and 2015 (1) extras before implementing.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c724913001mbUTbr7wUovJiq","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c71f6d10015kqXW5Evmy2rhC"}}
