":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The foundation is now validated against real-world truth:\n\n- **2019**: Flamengo champion with **90 pts (28W 6D 4L)** — EXACTLY matches the spec's example answer. Palmeiras 74 (21W 11D 6L) — matches spec exactly! Santos 74 (22W 8D 8L) — matches spec! Relegated 2019: Cruzeiro, Chapecoense, CSA, Avai ✓ (real truth).\n- **2020**: Flamengo 71, Inter 70, Atlético-MG 68 ✓ (real 2020 table). Relegated: Vasco, Goiás, Coritiba, Botafogo ✓ (real truth).\n- Serie A per season: 380 for all 2006-2022 (except tiny known holes 2009: 379, 2015: 381, 2023: 377) ✓.\n- Fla-Flu 2023: 4 matches (2 Copa + 2 Série A) ✓.\n\nFoundation is solid. Note \"Flamengo 2-0 Fluminense 2023-06-02 Copa\" — the spec example said \"2023-09-03: Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense\" — that exact match isn't in the data (spec example is illustrative, not ground truth). Fine.\n\nNow todo: mark foundation tasks complete, write queries.py + formatting.py + mcp_server.py + server.py, then tests. Let me now write queries.py — the full query engine. Design:\n\n```python\n# queries.py\nDERBIES = [\n    (\"Fla-Flu\", \"Flamengo\", \"Fluminense\"),\n    (\"Clássico dos Milhões\", \"Flamengo\", \"Vasco\"),\n    (\"Clássico Majestoso\", \"Corinthians\", \"Palmeiras\"),\n    (\"Choque-Rei\", \"Corinthians\", \"São Paulo\"),\n    (\"San-São\", \"Santos\", \"São Paulo\"),\n    (\"GreNal\", \"Grêmio\", \"Internacional\"),\n    (\"Atletiba\", \"Athletico Paranaense\", \"Coritiba\"),\n    (\"Ba-Vi\", \"Bahia\", \"Vitória\"),\n]\n```\nTeam names resolved via registry at query time.\n\nMethods on SoccerData (put queries in queries.py as functions taking SoccerData, or as methods? Cleaner: extend SoccerData via methods in queries.py? Python: define functions in queries.py that take `sd`. But discoverability... I'll put the query methods directly in queries.py as a mixin-like set of module functions, and have SoccerData methods delegate? Simpler: put ALL query methods on SoccerData in data.py? data.py is already long. I'll write queries.py with functions that accept SoccerData. MCP server calls these functions. Tests too. Hmm — actually a cleaner structure: make queries.py define a `QueryEngine` class that wraps SoccerData with the domain methods. But SoccerData already has some convenience methods... Let me just extend SoccerData with the full query API directly in queries.py via monkey... no. \n\nDecision: `queries.py` module with free functions taking `sd: SoccerData` as first arg. Clear, testable, no class gymnastics.\n\nFunctions:\n- resolve_team(sd, name) -> (key, display) or raise TeamNotFound w/ candidates\n- find_matches(sd, team=None, opponent=None, competition=None, season=None, date_from=None, date_to=None, stage=None, limit=None) -> list[Match]\n- last_match(sd, team, opponent=None) -> Match|None\n- head_to_head(sd, a, b, competition=None, season=None) -> dict\n- team_stats(sd, team, season=None, competition=None, venue='all') -> dict (incl home/away breakdown)\n- team_competitions(sd, team) -> list[dict]\n- standings(sd, competition='serie_a', season=None) -> list[TableRow]; default season = latest\n- relegation(sd, competition='serie_a', season=None, n=4) -> list[TableRow]\n- competition_info(sd, competition=None) -> dict\n- search_players(sd, name=None, nationality=None, club=None, position=None, min_overall=None, max_overall=None, limit=20) -> list[Player]\n- club_overview(sd, nationality='Brazil') -> list[dict] (Brazilian players at Brazilian clubs)\n- avg_goals(sd, competition=None, season=None) -> dict\n- biggest_wins(sd, competition=None, season=None, team=None, limit=10) -> list[Match]\n- best_records(sd, venue='home', competition=None, season=None, min_matches=10) -> list[dict]\n- derbies(sd, season=None, competition=None) -> list[(name, [Match])]\n- data_summary(sd) -> dict\n\nErrors: define `QueryError` with message for: unknown team (with candidates), non-league standings request, unknown competition, no data for season.\n\nResolution semantics for tools: `resolve_team` returns best candidate; if ambiguous (multiple strong), still pick best but tools add note. I'll return (key, note) where note = alternatives text if >1 candidate.\n\nLet me write queries.py now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c73b6b5001OU1mbVQBvVuuWb","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c7377ef001pHVunNrDGeyROG"}}
