C Bahia\", \"Fortaleza FC\", \"America MG\" displays — those come from most-frequent-raw picks. Slightly inconsistent prettiness but acceptable... Actually \"Fortaleza FC\" vs \"Fortaleza EC\" — both raw variants exist; count picked \"FC\"? Hmm — \"Fortaleza FC\" raw count vs \"Fortaleza EC\"... whichever. Acceptable.\n6. `search_matches` note \"Flamengo do Piauí-PI (4)\" — good disambiguation note.\n7. Also note `Palmeiras matches 2023` — 2023 coverage from BRF ✓.\n\nAlso `head_to_head` shows \"2020-01-30: Palmeiras 1-0 Santos (Copa Libertadores final)\" — the 2020 LIB final single leg ✓ correct!\n\nNow fix the two formatting nits (title with competition display, best_records label). Then write the test suite.\n\nFix 1 — in `search_matches` tool: title_bits.append(q._resolve_competition(competition) or competition) → append COMPETITIONS display:\n```python\nif competition:\n    code = q._resolve_competition(competition)\n    title_bits.append(COMPETITIONS.get(code, competition))\n```\n\nFix 2 — best_records call: `fmt.format_best_records(ranked, venue, label or \" (whole dataset)\")` — change to pass label=\"whole dataset\" and handle in formatter. The formatter does f\"Best {venue_text} records {label}:\" — so pass label=\"\" → \"Best away records :\" bad. Let me restructure: build label as string; if empty → no scope; formatter: f\"Best {venue_text} records{(' ' + label) if label else ''}:\". I'll adjust formatter to accept label and prepend space properly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c76b462001vACG2JB7LBV9bX","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c7691e9001kqUqkxSCY4NU52"}}
