{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788257773548,"sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9fc1571fadb2409b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brsoccer.data import load_default\nfrom brsoccer import queries as q\n\nsd = load_default()\nprint(\"resolve Bahia ->\", sd.registry.resolve(\"Bahia\")[:2] and [(r.key, r.display, r.match_count) for r in sd.registry.resolve(\"Bahia\")])\nprint(\"resolve Vitória ->\", [(r.key, r.display, r.match_count) for r in sd.registry.resolve(\"Vitória\")][:4])\nprint(\"key_of 'Vitória' =\", sd.registry.key_of(\"Vitória\"))\nprint(\"key_of 'EC Vitoria' =\", sd.registry.key_of(\"EC Vitoria\"))\nprint(\"key_of 'Vitória - BA' =\", sd.registry.key_of(\"Vitória - BA\"))\nprint(\"key_of 'Vitoria ES' =\", sd.registry.key_of(\"Vitoria ES\"))\n# what keys contain 'vitoria'\nprint(\"registry vitoria keys:\", [(k, e.display, e.match_count) for k, e in sd.registry.entries.items() if 'vitoria' in k])\n# Bahia 2023 matches vs vitoria?\nb = q.resolve_team(sd, \"Bahia\")\nv = q.resolve_team(sd, \"Vitória\")\nbv = [m for m in sd.matches if m.season==2023 and m.is_between(b, v)]\nprint(\"Ba-Vi 2023:\", [(str(m.date), m.home_display, m.score_text, m.away_display, m.competition) for m in bv])\n# all 2023 serie_b matches involving vitoria\nvms = [m for m in sd.matches_for_team(v) if m.season == 2023]\nprint(\"Vitória 2023 matches:\", len(vms))\nprint(\"Bahia key display:\", sd.team_display(b))\nEOF"},"output":"resolve Bahia -> [('bahia', 'EC Bahia', 1079), ('bahia de feira', 'Bahia de Feira-BA', 10)]\nresolve Vitória -> [('vitoria ba', 'Vitória', 1028), ('vitoria da conquista', 'Vitória da Conquista-BA', 14), ('vitoria es', 'Vitoria ES', 3), ('vitoria f c', 'Vitoria F. C.-ES', 2)]\nkey_of 'Vitória' = vitoria ba\nkey_of 'EC Vitoria' = vitoria ba\nkey_of 'Vitória - BA' = vitoria ba\nkey_of 'Vitoria ES' = vitoria es\nregistry vitoria keys: [('vitoria ba', 'Vitória', 1028), ('vitoria da conquista', 'Vitória da Conquista-BA', 14), ('vitoria f c', 'Vitoria F. C.-ES', 2), ('vitoria es', 'Vitoria ES', 3)]\nBa-Vi 2023: []\nVitória 2023 matches: 39\nBahia key display: EC Bahia\n","metadata":{"output":"resolve Bahia -> [('bahia', 'EC Bahia', 1079), ('bahia de feira', 'Bahia de Feira-BA', 10)]\nresolve Vitória -> [('vitoria ba', 'Vitória', 1028), ('vitoria da conquista', 'Vitória da Conquista-BA', 14), ('vitoria es', 'Vitoria ES', 3), ('vitoria f c', 'Vitoria F. C.-ES', 2)]\nkey_of 'Vitória' = vitoria ba\nkey_of 'EC Vitoria' = vitoria ba\nkey_of 'Vitória - BA' = vitoria ba\nkey_of 'Vitoria ES' = vitoria es\nregistry vitoria keys: [('vitoria ba', 'Vitória', 1028), ('vitoria da conquista', 'Vitória da Conquista-BA', 14), ('vitoria f c', 'Vitoria F. C.-ES', 2), ('vitoria es', 'Vitoria ES', 3)]\nBa-Vi 2023: []\nVitória 2023 matches: 39\nBahia key display: EC Bahia\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brsoccer.data import load_default\nfrom brsoccer import queries as q\n\nsd = load_default()\nprint(\"resolve Bahia ->\", sd.registry.resolve(\"Bahia\")[:2] and [(r.key, r.display, r.match_count) for r in sd.registry.resolve(\"Bahia\")])\nprint(\"resolve Vitória ->\", [(r.key, r.display, r.match_count) for r in sd.registry.resolve(\"Vitória\")][:4])\nprint(\"key_of 'Vitória' =\", sd.registry.key_of(\"Vitória\"))\nprint(\"key_of 'EC Vitoria' =\", sd.registry.key_of(\"EC Vitoria\"))\nprint(\"key_of 'Vitória - BA' =\", sd.registry.key_of(\"Vitória - BA\"))\nprint(\"key_of 'Vitoria ES' =\", sd.registry.key_of(\"Vitoria ES\"))\n# what keys contain 'vitoria'\nprint(\"registry vitoria keys:\", [(k, e.display, e.match_count) for k, e in sd.registry.entries.items() if 'vitoria' in k])\n# Bahia 2023 matches vs vitoria?\nb = q.resolve_team(sd, \"Bahia\")\nv = q.resolve_team(sd, \"Vitória\")\nbv = [m for m in sd.matches if m.season==2023 and m.is_between(b, v)]\nprint(\"Ba-Vi 2023:\", [(str(m.date), m.home_display, m.score_text, m.away_display, m.competition) for m in bv])\n# all 2023 serie_b matches involving vitoria\nvms = [m for m in sd.matches_for_team(v) if m.season == 2023]\nprint(\"Vitória 2023 matches:\", len(vms))\nprint(\"Bahia key display:\", sd.team_display(b))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788257773531,"end":1788257773547}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All facts gathered. Note: 2023 standings from the partial 377-match data show Grêmio on top (68 pts) — because the data is missing 3 matches and possibly some rounds for certain teams; the real 2023 champion was Palmeiras. So for 2023 tests I should NOT assert \"Palmeiras champion\" — the dataset is what it is. I'll assert structure (table has 20 teams, top team exists, points ordering desc) rather than real-world facts for 2023. Also note \"most goals 2023: Grêmio 63\" — same partial-data caveat; the spec question \"Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023?\" can still be ANSWERED (answer per dataset: Grêmio) — for the sample-questions test I'll assert the answer exists (contains a team name) not a specific real-world value. For 2019 (complete data) I can assert real truth.\n\n\"M. Barbosa\" GK at Villarreal — the Gabriel Barbosa fallback also matches Barbosa — fine, both are honest candidates.\n\nInteresting: Corinthians 2022 home record = 19 matches, 12W 4D 3L, 24 GF, 11 GA, 63.2% — the spec example said 11W 5D 3L 28:15 57.9% (illustrative). My data-derived numbers differ from the spec's illustrative example — the spec example is explicitly example-format, and our numbers come from the actual dataset. For the BDD test I assert the actual computed values (19 matches, 12/4/3, 24/11).\n\nAlso derbies 2023: Ba-Vi missing (Bahia/Vitória not both in 2023 Serie A — Bahia yes, Vitória in Série B 2023 → no Ba-Vi in 2023 serie_a; Vitória IS in serie_b 2023 — but derbies() searches ALL matches (no competition filter) — Ba-Vi didn't appear because... derbies() searches all sd.matches with season 2023 — Bahia vs Vitória in 2023? Série B has Bahia AND Vitória 2023! They'd meet twice. Hmm — Ba-Vi not in the list... why? Let me think: derbies() resolves \"Bahia\" and \"Vitória\" via resolve_team. \"Vitória\" → key? Vitória-BA — is \"vitoria\" ambiguous? Earlier analysis: vitoria ufs {ES} suffixed... wait BRF has \"Vitoria ES\" AND \"EC Vitoria\"/\"Vitoria\" (BA). Is there \"Vitória - BA\" in COPA? If yes → ambiguous {BA, ES} → keys \"vitoria ba\" / \"vitoria es\"; bare \"Vitoria\" (BRF/FIFA) → dominance → \"vitoria ba\" probably (EC Vitoria count ~300 vs Vitoria ES few) — so resolve(\"Vitória\") → \"vitoria ba\" ✓. And Bahia 2023 Série B matches vs \"vitoria ba\"... IF the BRF Serie B 2023 rows spell Vitória as \"EC Vitoria\" → key \"vitoria ba\" ✓ — then Ba-Vi matches SHOULD be found. Unless resolve(\"Vitória\") returned \"vitoria es\"! Dominance counts: \"Vitoria ES\" (BRF Serie C/D?) vs \"EC Vitoria\"/\"Vitoria\" (Série B/A appearances ~hundreds). Dominance should be BA... unless \"EC Vitoria\" got keyed differently! \"EC Vitoria\" → strip ec → \"vitoria\" — bare ambiguous → dominance → \"vitoria ba\"?? Only if _base_uf_counts[\"vitoria\"][\"BA\"] exists — which requires some raw with \"vitoria\" + uf BA (e.g. \"Vitória - BA\" in COPA). If NO raw ever has \"Vitória - BA\", then base \"vitoria\" has only uf {ES} → NOT ambiguous → bare \"Vitoria\"/\"EC Vitoria\" → key \"vitoria\" (no uf!). Then resolve(\"Vitória\") → \"vitoria\" ✓ and Serie B matches use \"vitoria\" ✓ they'd match. Hmm then why no Ba-Vi in 2023?\n\nLet me check: does 2023 Serie B data contain Bahia vs Vitória? The 2023 Série B: Bahia and Vitória both played (real). BRF Serie B 2023 has 380 matches ✓ complete. So Ba-Vi should exist... unless the derby resolution failed. Let me debug resolve(\"Bahia\"), resolve(\"Vitória\") and their 2023 Série B matches.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c781335001Pn9sIHmmCBPkwu","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLM