 > 1 and tokens[0].lower() in LEADING_DESIGNATORS:\n+        tokens.pop(0)\n+    while len(tokens) > 1 and tokens[-1].lower() in TRAILING_DESIGNATORS:\n+        tokens.pop()\n+    return \" \".join(tokens)\n \n def resolve(self, query: str, limit: int = 8) -> list[Resolution]:\n     \"\"\"Rank canonical teams matching a user query.\n \n","additions":8,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brsoccer/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788257795038,"end":1788257795040}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Vitória resolves correctly (\"vitoria ba\", 1028 matches, 39 matches in 2023). But Ba-Vi 2023 = [] — Bahia and Vitória never met in 2023 in the data. Reality check: 2023 Série B — Bahia and Vitória both played Série B 2023... wait, actually NO: **Bahia was in Série A 2023** (promoted after 2022 Série B), and **Vitória was in Série B 2023**. So they did NOT meet in 2023 — the data is CORRECT, my expectation was wrong! Ba-Vi derby needs both in the same division. In which seasons does Ba-Vi exist in the data? Bahia & Vitória both in Série A 2010-2011(?), 2013(?), 2014... Ba-Vi matches exist in earlier seasons. Fine — the derbies tool works; 2023 just has no Ba-Vi. For the test, use 2019 or a season where Ba-Vi exists — or just assert derbies(2019) includes Ba-Vi? 2019 Série A: Bahia yes, Vitória yes (2019 Série A had Vitória ✓ relegated 2019? Vitória relegated 2019? hmm Vitória was relegated in 2019? No — Vitória relegated 2018... 2019 Série A teams included Bahia and... let me just check Ba-Vi seasons in data during test-writing; the derbies(season=None) full-data test will include all.\n\nAlso note display \"EC Bahia\" — meh. \"EC Bahia\" comes from BRF raw \"EC Bahia\" being the most frequent variant. HIST has \"Bahia\" bare... display pick = max count → BRF \"EC Bahia\" (designator retained in display). Cosmetic improvement: in _pick_display, strip leading/trailing designator tokens and trailing UF-ish from the DISPLAY? But display for ambiguous keys should KEEP UF (\"Botafogo-PB\"). Current display \"Botafogo-RJ\" ✓ good. For \"EC Bahia\" → strip \"EC \" prefix → \"Bahia\" nicer. Rule: strip leading/trailing designators from display (safe — purely cosmetic); keep internal hyphens/UF. Let me add that to _pick_display: after picking best raw, remove leading/trailing standalone designator tokens (case-insensitive via preprocess? careful — display is the ORIGINAL-cased string; strip tokens case-insensitively but preserve rest).\n\nImplement: tokens = display.split(); while tokens and tokens[0].lower() in LEADING_DESIGNATORS: pop(0); while tokens and tokens[-1].lower() in TRAILING_DESIGNATORS: pop(). Join. \"EC Bahia\" → \"Bahia\" ✓. \"Fortaleza FC\" → \"Fortaleza\" ✓. \"America MG\" stays \"America MG\" (hmm — display for 'america mg'... raw winner by count: BRF \"America MG\"? → display \"America MG\". COPA has \"América - MG\" → dash-collapsed \"América-MG\". Count: BRF ~200+ vs COPA ~40 → \"America MG\". Acceptable. \"Sport Club do Recife\" — not picked (alias target \"sport\" winner is \"Sport-PE\" → \"Sport-PE\"?? display for key \"sport\": raws \"Sport-PE\" (BRAS ~250), \"Sport Recife\" (BRF ~100), \"Sport Club do Recife\" (FIFA 20) → winner \"Sport-PE\" → dash collapse → \"Sport-PE\". Hmm — \"Sport-PE\" as display is fine (unambiguous-ish). Actually BRAS \"Sport-PE\" count ~ 2012-2022 appearances... vs BRF \"Sport Recife\" ~150, HIST \"Sport\" bare (2003-2019 ~300!) — wait HIST bare \"Sport\" would win by count → display \"Sport\" ✓ nicer. HIST teams list showed 'Sport' hmm — the HIST team list printed earlier: ['América-MG', 'América-RN', 'Athletico-PR', 'Atlético-GO', 'Atlético-MG', 'Avaí', 'Bahia', 'Barueri', 'Brasiliense', 'CSA', 'Ceará', 'Chapecoense', 'Corinthians', 'Coritiba'] — 'Sport' should be in HIST (Sport-PE in Série A 2003-2019 occasionally: 2012, 2015, 2016...). Bare counts for \"sport\"... earlier \"top bare names\" list: didn't show 'sport' in top 20 but it's there somewhere below 527. BRF \"Sport Recife\" ~250 + BRAS \"Sport-PE\" ~100 + HIST \"Sport\" ~80 + FIFA 20 → winner probably \"Sport Recife\" → display \"Sport Recife\" ✓ fine.\n\nOK — implement the designator-strip in _pick_display. Then write all the tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c786d9d001NYa9sTXEvDZCyu","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c782944001PScSeMctI4B03q"}}
