{"type":"text","timestamp":1788258029992,"sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","part":{"id":"prt_05c7becd2001HSQLNT7sPWgGZf","messageID":"msg_05c7bbb84001RtqpBGTYe1NvBJ","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","type":"text","text":"The tools must catch `QueryError` and return friendly text instead of protocol errors. Refactoring with a `@register` decorator:","time":{"start":1788258020562,"end":1788258029991}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788258029998,"sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bafae0521da08499","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-ad7c1ce592bf/brsoccer/mcp_server.py","newString":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sys\nimport threading\nfrom functools import wraps\n\nfrom mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\n\nfrom . import formatting as fmt\nfrom . import queries as q\nfrom .data import COMPETITIONS, SoccerData, load_default\n\n_DATA: SoccerData | None = None\n_LOAD_LOCK = threading.Lock()\n\n\ndef _soccer_data() -> SoccerData:\n    \"\"\"Load the datasets once (thread-safe, lazy).\"\"\"\n    global _DATA\n    if _DATA is None:\n        with _LOAD_LOCK:\n            if _DATA is None:\n                print(\"[brsoccer] loading datasets ...\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n                _DATA = load_default()\n                print(\n                    f\"[brsoccer] loaded {_DATA.matches and len(_DATA.matches)} matches, \"\n                    f\"{len(_DATA.players)} players, {len(_DATA.registry.entries)} teams\",\n                    file=sys.stderr,\n                    flush=True,\n                )\n    return _DATA\n\n\ndef _note_for(name: str | None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Append disambiguation note when a team query matched several clubs.\"\"\"\n    if not name:\n        return \"\"\n    note = q.alternatives_note(_soccer_data(), name)\n    return f\"\\n{note}\" if note else \"\"\n\n\ndef _friendly_errors(fn):\n    \"\"\"Turn QueryError into guidance text instead of a protocol error.\"\"\"\n\n    @wraps(fn)\n    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n        try:\n            return fn(*args, **kwargs)\n        except q.QueryError as err:\n            return f\"Cannot answer this question with the available data: {err}\"\n\n    return wrapper\n\n\ndef build_server(data: SoccerData | None = None) -> MCPServer:\n    \"\"\"Construct the MCPServer with all tools registered.\"\"\"\n    if data is not None:\n        global _DATA\n        _DATA = data\n\n    server = MCPServer(\n        name=\"brazilian-soccer\",\n        title=\"Brazilian Soccer Knowledge Server\",\n        description=(\n            \"Natural-language-ready queries about Brazilian soccer: matches, teams, \"\n            \"players, competitions and statistics, from Kaggle datasets covering the \"\n            \"Brasileirao (2003-2023), Copa do Brasil (2012-2023), Copa Libertadores \"\n            \"(2013-2022) and a FIFA player database.\"\n        ),\n    )\n\n    def register(fn):\n        \"\"\"Combined decorator: friendly errors + MCP registration.\"\"\"\n        return server.tool()(_friendly_errors(fn))","oldString":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sys\nimport threading\n\nfrom mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\n\nfrom . import formatting as fmt\nfrom . import queries as q\nfrom .data import COMPETITIONS, SoccerData, load_default\n\n_DATA: SoccerData | None = None\n_LOAD_LOCK = threading.Lock()\n\n\ndef _soccer_data() -> SoccerData:\n    \"\"\"Load the datasets once (thread-safe, lazy).\"\"\"\n    global _DATA\n    if _DATA is None:\n        with _LOAD_LOCK:\n            if _DATA is None:\n                print(\"[brsoccer] loading datasets ...\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n                _DATA = load_default()\n                print(\n                    f\"[brsoccer] loaded {_DATA.matches and len(_DATA.matches)} matches, \"\n                    f\"{len(_DATA.players)} players, {len(_DATA.registry.entries)} teams\",\n                    file=sys.stderr,\n                    flush=True,\n                )\n    return _DATA\n\n\ndef _note_for(name: str | None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Append disambiguation note when a team query matched several clubs.\"\"\"\n    if not name:\n        return \"\"\n    note = q.alternatives_note(_soccer_data(), name)\n    return f\"\\n{note}\" if note else \"\"\n\n\ndef build_server(data: SoccerData | None = None) -> MCPServer:\n    \"\"\"Construct the MCPServer with all tools registered.\"\"\"\n    if data is not None:\n        global _DATA\n        _DATA = data\n\n    server = MCPServer(\n        name=\"brazilian-soccer\",\n        title=\"Brazilian Soccer Knowledge Server\",\n        description=(\n            \"Natural-language-ready queries about Brazilian soccer: matches, teams, \"\n            \"players, competitions and statistics, from Kaggle datasets covering the \"\n            \"Brasileirao (2003-2023), Copa do Brasil (2012-2023), Copa Libertadores \"\n            \"(2013-2022) and a FIFA player database.\"\n        ),\n    )"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-ad7c1ce592bf/brsoccer/mcp_server.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-ad7c1ce592bf/brsoccer/mcp_server.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-ad7c1ce592bf/brsoccer/mcp_server.py\n@@ -17,8 +17,9 @@\n from __future__ import annotations\n \n import sys\n import threading\n+from functools import wraps\n \n from mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\n \n from . import formatting as fmt\n@@ -53,8 +54,21 @@\n     note = q.alternatives_note(_soccer_data(), name)\n     return f\"\\n{note}\" if note else \"\"\n \n \n+def _friendly_errors(fn):\n+    \"\"\"Turn QueryError into guidance text instead of a protocol error.\"\"\"\n+\n+    @wraps(fn)\n+    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n+        try:\n+            return fn(*args, **kwargs)\n+        except q.QueryError as err:\n+            return f\"Cannot answer this question with the available data: {err}\"\n+\n+    return wrapper\n+\n+\n def build_server(data: SoccerData | None = None) -> MCPServer:\n     \"\"\"Construct the MCPServer with all tools registered.\"\"\"\n     if data is not None:\n         global _DATA\n@@ -70,8 +84,12 @@\n             \"(2013-2022) and a FIFA player database.\"\n         ),\n     )\n \n+    def register(fn):\n+        \"\"\"Combined decorator: friendly errors + MCP registration.\"\"\"\n+        return server.tool()(_friendly_errors(fn))\n+\n     # ------------------------------------------------------------ team tools\n \n     @server.tool()\n     def find_team(name: str) -> str:\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-ad7c1ce592bf/brsoccer/mcp_server.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-ad7c1ce592bf/brsoccer/mcp_server.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-ad7c1ce592bf/brsoccer/mcp_server.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-ad7c1ce592bf/brsoccer/mcp_server.py\n@@ -17,8 +17,9 @@\n from __future__ import annotations\n \n import sys\n import threading\n+from functools import wraps\n \n from mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\n \n from . import formatting as fmt\n@@ -53,8 +54,21 @@\n     note = q.alternatives_note(_soccer_data(), name)\n     return f\"\\n{note}\" if note else \"\"\n \n \n+def _friendly_errors(fn):\n+    \"\"\"Turn QueryError into guidance text instead of a protocol error.\"\"\"\n+\n+    @wraps(fn)\n+    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n+        try:\n+            return fn(*args, **kwargs)\n+        except q.QueryError as err:\n+            return f\"Cannot answer this question with the available data: {err}\"\n+\n+    return wrapper\n+\n+\n def build_server(data: SoccerData | None = None) -> MCPServer:\n     \"\"\"Construct the MCPServer with all tools registered.\"\"\"\n     if data is not None:\n         global _DATA\n@@ -70,8 +84,12 @@\n             \"(2013-2022) and a FIFA player database.\"\n         ),\n     )\n \n+    def register(fn):\n+        \"\"\"Combined decorator: friendly errors + MCP registration.\"\"\"\n+        return server.tool()(_friendly_errors(fn))\n+\n     # ------------------------------------------------------------ team tools\n \n     @server.tool()\n     def find_team(name: str) -> str:\n","additions":18,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brsoccer/mcp_server.py","time":{"start":1788258029994,"end":1788258029996}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — `test_unknown_team_returns_friendly_guidance`: my MCP tools don't catch QueryError! The tool functions call q.team_stats which raises QueryError → the SDK will return an error result (isError=True) with the exception message. Hmm — the test asserts `not result.isError` and \"No team found\" in text. Which behavior do I have? The tools as written DON'T catch exceptions — so the SDK converts them to tool errors. The message would still contain \"No team found...\" as the error text presumably. Two options:\n\n(a) Catch QueryError in tools and return friendly text as normal results.\n(b) Let them be protocol errors with message text.\n\nThe spec says \"Returns properly formatted responses\" and \"No timeout errors\". For LLM ergonomics, friendly text (a) is better — the model sees guidance rather than an exception. Let me add a decorator in mcp_server that wraps each tool function to catch QueryError and return \"No data found: <msg>\" style text. Cleanest: a helper `_safe(fn)` wrapper applied in each tool... that's invasive. Alternative: wrap the whole build_server tool registration — define a local decorator:\n\n```python\ndef _friendly(tool_fn):\n    @functools.wraps(tool_fn)\n    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n        try:\n            return tool_fn(*args, **kwargs)\n        except q.QueryError as err:\n            return f\"Cannot answer: {err}\"\n    return wrapper\n```\n\nBut the SDK's @server.tool() decorator inspects the function signature for the schema — wrapping AFTER registration is fine if I apply _friendly BEFORE @server.tool(): i.e. `@server.tool()` on top of `@_friendly`. functools.wraps preserves signature via __wrapped__ — does the SDK inspect signature correctly through wraps? inspect.signature follows __wrapped__ ✓. The docstring is preserved ✓.\n\nHmm — but there's a subtlety: the SDK may register by function __name__ ✓ preserved by wraps.\n\nLet me restructure: in build_server, define `def tool(fn)` combined decorator:\n```python\nfrom functools import wraps\ndef _friendly_error(fn):\n    @wraps(fn)\n    def wrapper(*a, **kw):\n        try:\n            return fn(*a, **kw)\n        except QueryError as err:\n            return f\"Cannot answer this question with the available data: {err}\"\n    return wrapper\n```\nand apply `@server.tool()` `@_friendly_error` on each tool. That's 16 edits... Alternatively apply inside a small helper `register = lambda fn: server.tool()(_friendly_error(fn))` and use `@register` on each tool — one-line change per tool anyway. Hmm, all 16 tools already have `@server.tool()` — I'd need to edit each. Use sed-like replaceAll: replace \"@server.tool()\" with \"@register\" and define register once. Let me do that with replaceAll edit.\n\nAlso update the stdio test to assert the friendly path (isError False, \"Cannot answer\" prefix? I wrote \"No team found\" in text — with (a) the text = \"Cannot answer this question with the available data: No team found for 'Manchester United'. Try one of: ...\" ✓ contains \"No team found\" ✓. And standings la liga → \"Cannot answer ...: Unknown competition 'la liga'...\" ✓ contains \"Unknown competition\" ✓.\n\nAlso the sample-questions test asserts `result.is_error is False` in call_tool helper — with friendly errors, all good. But NOTE: \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" expects the custom gap message ✓ already handled.\n\nOne more consideration — the in-process server tests use `server.call_tool` — QueryError-caught text flows the same ✓.\n\nNow performance test file.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c7bee9900142TCOHLQtqDxwy","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","messageID":"msg_05c7bbb84001RtqpBGTYe1NvBJ"}}
