{"type":"text","timestamp":1788258387411,"sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","part":{"id":"prt_05c817142001h3o04e0P2Hk0ER","messageID":"msg_05c81631d001G6YBRic6i7E6CO","sessionID":"ses_fa39bca00ffeV1iObla3wLMRAJ","type":"text","text":"Complete. Implemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP server per TASK.md:\n\n**Code** (all in the current directory):\n- `brsoccer/` — query engine: `normalize.py` (team canonicalization across all naming variants: state suffixes, accents, `A.b.c. - RN` dotted forms, `Red Bull Bragantino`, FIFA's `América FC (Minas Gerais)`; ambiguity detection for Santos-SP/AP, Botafogo-RJ/PB/SP etc.), `dates.py` (ISO/ISO+time/Brazilian formats, `NA`/`-` sentinels), `data.py` (loads all 6 CSVs, cross-file dedupe — the two Brasileirão files overlap 2012-2019, BR-Football overlaps 2014-2023 with ±1-day date drift; league rows dated Jan/Feb attributed to the prior season for the pandemic-delayed 2020), `queries.py` (matches, h2h, team stats with home/away splits, computed standings/relegation, player search with FIFA-club↔match-team join, aggregates, derbies), `formatting.py`, `mcp_server.py` (16 MCP tools, official `mcp` SDK v2, stdio)\n- `server.py` entry point, `pyproject.toml` (`pip install -e .` + `brsoccer-mcp` console script), `tests/` (9 BDD files)\n\n**Verification**:\n- 134 tests pass (`pytest`), ~92% coverage — BDD Given/When/Then scenarios for all 5 spec capability categories, 25 spec sample questions answered end-to-end, real MCP stdio client↔server integration, latency guards (<2s simple / <5s aggregate)\n- Data validated against known truth: 2019 standings compute to Flamengo 90 pts (28W 6D 4L) — exactly the spec's example — 2020 relegation (Vasco/Goiás/Coritiba/Botafogo), every season 2006–2022 dedupes to exactly 380 matches\n- Raw JSON-RPC stdio handshake and `brsoccer-mcp` entry point verified","time":{"start":1788258382146,"end":1788258387408}}}
